WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Genie 4 now gives builders real-time physics, reasoning, and audio, and interactive simulations they can test today. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 217. Instruction 2 Number Habits, new Icelandic encoders, and an open medical decision model come next. Then things to try. DeepMind has begun rolling Genie 4 out to trusted testers, the lab said. The interactive world model nest simulations inside other simulations. It builds on prior Genie versions by adding richer sensory and planning capability.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.900
that let users create and interact with dynamic environments.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:39.320
Developers and researchers interested in simulation, robotics, or game-like world building

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.840
can sign up on a wait list with wider access plans soon.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.380
The model runs at interactive speeds.

00:00:46.471 --> 00:00:48.831
Instruction-tuning installs round number avoidance

00:00:49.071 --> 00:00:50.831
and sharpens endpoint avoidance,

00:00:51.231 --> 00:00:55.111
making number distributions less uniform according to a paper on archive.

00:00:55.611 --> 00:00:59.651
The comparison used 15 matched base and tuned open-weight model pairs.

00:00:59.651 --> 00:01:07.391
base models return the N.1 and N at 0.30 to 0.60 of the interior rate, while

00:01:07.391 --> 00:01:12.311
tuned models almost never do. Tune models also avoid multiples of 10 almost

00:01:12.311 --> 00:01:18.291
completely. The study evaluated 18 model lines at 5 ranges up to N equals 100

00:01:18.291 --> 00:01:24.171
under 29 decoding configurations. No shared model integer above N equals 10 showed

00:01:24.171 --> 00:01:27.171
up across more than 42% of tuned conditions.

00:01:28.108 --> 00:01:33.688
Iceland now has open data modern-burt encoders trained for the language, including a from-scratch

00:01:33.688 --> 00:01:35.608
model and a warm start from English.

00:01:36.168 --> 00:01:41.868
The 1 billion-parameter model trained from scratch on 9 billion open tokens outperforms

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:45.248
the prior iceberg reference on all 11 evaluated tasks.

00:01:45.728 --> 00:01:50.788
A warm-started version from an English-etting encoder of the same shape ranks highest on

00:01:50.788 --> 00:01:51.488
every task.

00:01:51.488 --> 00:01:56.888
Warm start transfer from English layers works at base size and above even when the target

00:01:56.888 --> 00:01:58.768
vocabulary is transplanted.

00:01:58.988 --> 00:02:03.808
The 1 billion parameter model remains the first model lingual Icelandic encoder of that

00:02:03.808 --> 00:02:04.228
scale.

00:02:05.305 --> 00:02:11.205
Medgev is an open system 1 model, fast, intuitive decision making that runs locally on a laptop.

00:02:11.825 --> 00:02:20.505
It reaches 72.5% on MedQA, 75.4% on the United States Medical Licensing Examination, or USMLE,

00:02:20.505 --> 00:02:25.185
and 80.1% on the New England Journal of Medicine or NEJM.

00:02:25.765 --> 00:02:30.745
Expected calibration error, a measure of how well confidence matches accuracy, stays

00:02:30.745 --> 00:02:35.405
within 0.028-0.063 on those knowledge tasks.

00:02:35.885 --> 00:02:43.045
On patient-level prediction from MIMIC4, it exceeds XG boost on in-hospital mortality with

00:02:43.045 --> 00:02:48.605
an area under the receiver operating curve or AUROC of 0.926.

00:02:48.605 --> 00:02:54.105
6, but trails supervise models on operational outcomes such as emergency department triage

00:02:54.105 --> 00:02:54.605
admission.

00:02:55.145 --> 00:03:01.445
A 2-parameter recalibration method using 50-200 local labels reduces expected calibration

00:03:01.445 --> 00:03:05.105
error to 0.007 on patient-level tasks.

00:03:06.068 --> 00:03:11.648
Manipulation and navigation share one high-level decision model in OmniBrain-0, a lightweight

00:03:11.648 --> 00:03:13.168
unified embodied agent.

00:03:13.168 --> 00:03:18.888
Training uses embodied pre-training, domain specialized distillation, and multi-teacher

00:03:18.888 --> 00:03:20.348
on-policy distillation.

00:03:20.888 --> 00:03:25.828
Rubric guided recursive self-improvement turns execution evidence into refined rubric's

00:03:25.828 --> 00:03:28.468
and verified trajectories before reconsolidation.

00:03:29.028 --> 00:03:38.848
Evaluation covers Libero Pro Robocassa 365, Robo Twin 2.0, R2RCE, and multiple real-world

00:03:38.848 --> 00:03:43.888
manipulation tasks. Inference and execution overhead come in substantially lower than

00:03:43.888 --> 00:03:51.543
its closed-source teacher. Annual SEC 10K filings become inference time context in Fin LLMKG,

00:03:51.923 --> 00:03:57.023
which injects temporally grounded company-level facts into any causal large language model,

00:03:57.403 --> 00:04:03.263
or LLM, without weight updates. The framework supplies either natural language profiles or

00:04:03.263 --> 00:04:08.283
relevance-ranked triples. It attributes each sentiment score to individual sentences and

00:04:08.283 --> 00:04:13.343
retrieved triples for inspectability. Portfolio performance improves over state-of-the-art

00:04:13.343 --> 00:04:18.914
baselines in simulation. Agent handoffs now have a dedicated continuity test called

00:04:18.914 --> 00:04:26.434
the Handoff State Continuity Benchmark, or HSC-Bench. It contains 1,039 tasks that measure

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:32.014
how well a receiving model recovers repository evidence and continues from prior conversational,

00:04:32.314 --> 00:04:37.614
tool and file state. Structured Handoff State improves evidence recovery for every tested

00:04:37.614 --> 00:04:40.694
and model, and continuation performance for most models.

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.794
The strongest receivers differ between the two tracks.

00:04:44.791 --> 00:04:49.311
Traumem reframes agent memory as task-oriented role-adaptive workspaces.

00:04:49.771 --> 00:04:54.751
It organizes interaction histories into local threads and builds those workspaces by assigning

00:04:54.751 --> 00:05:00.291
roles and jointly selecting complementary memories across event, affect, and time views.

00:05:00.871 --> 00:05:07.751
On Locomo and Mem Gallery, it delivers macro-F1 gains of 2.23 to 3.14 points over

00:05:07.751 --> 00:05:14.431
prior memory systems. It uses 5.1 to 12.8% fewer context tokens on two backbones.

00:05:15.573 --> 00:05:20.493
Multilingual multi-hop document question answering gets a learned skill orchestration policy

00:05:20.493 --> 00:05:27.473
in doc skill. The policy is trained via bounded Monte Carlo tree search or MCTS, demonstrations

00:05:27.473 --> 00:05:33.513
and direct preference optimization or DPO, to select, revisit, or skip skills as evidence

00:05:33.513 --> 00:05:39.793
state evolves. On the new MMHAB doc bench of 60,000 question answer pairs across 10 languages,

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:49.453
the QN3 VL8B instantiation reaches 41.0 accuracy and 49.2 F1. That exceeds the strongest

00:05:49.453 --> 00:05:57.814
baseline by 5.5 and 6.3 points. Camer, short for compatibility aware memory replay, jointly controls

00:05:57.814 --> 00:06:03.054
current example supervision and historical replay for continual learning in large language models.

00:06:03.054 --> 00:06:08.794
Compatibility checks and a learned memory gate choose among learning with replay, reinforcing

00:06:08.794 --> 00:06:11.914
compatible examples or skipping mastered duplicates.

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:18.194
On wiki big edit, it reaches 93.66% original match after only 3,000 facts.

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:23.974
It leads all evaluated methods on four trace tasks while preserving earlier task performance.

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:30.533
Bengali speech research just got lipigore, a large-scale, diorized multi-domain corpus.

00:06:30.533 --> 00:06:37.733
It supplies 885 hours of speaker-diarrhized long-form audio from 998 YouTube videos across

00:06:37.733 --> 00:06:43.413
17 domains, together with SSTT annotations and a human verified gold split.

00:06:43.893 --> 00:06:48.793
The construction pipeline is released as reusable code for any language with captioned YouTube

00:06:48.793 --> 00:06:49.253
presence.

00:06:49.873 --> 00:06:56.413
For automatic speech recognition or ASR models, show consistent degradation on a motive, dialectal,

00:06:56.573 --> 00:06:57.793
and long-form content.

00:06:57.793 --> 00:07:04.136
Homo glyph and invisible character Watermark still leave across lingual fairness gap, even

00:07:04.136 --> 00:07:05.776
without a tokenizer in the loop.

00:07:06.356 --> 00:07:12.696
Capacity varies 3.3 fold across 40 language varieties and 24 scripts, with script accounting

00:07:12.696 --> 00:07:14.696
for 96% of the variation.

00:07:15.376 --> 00:07:20.576
Ordinary copypaste widens the gap so that a detector needs roughly two code points for English

00:07:20.576 --> 00:07:23.036
or Persian, but 93 for Lau.

00:07:23.036 --> 00:07:29.357
ETMM decouples and aligns heterogeneous memory for long-term conversational agents.

00:07:29.717 --> 00:07:35.177
It parses conversations into atomic units, separates effective information, and maintains

00:07:35.177 --> 00:07:41.517
three hierarchical views, event, affect, and time, with adaptively calibrated thresholds.

00:07:41.877 --> 00:07:50.677
On locomo and long-mem Eval S, it improves accuracy by 12.46% and 7.96% relative to state-of-the-art

00:07:50.677 --> 00:07:57.154
baselines, while keeping competitive token efficiency. An embedding-based retrieval plus LLM

00:07:57.154 --> 00:08:03.794
filtering approach now hunts evidence inside a large randomized evaluation corpus. It finds 92%

00:08:03.794 --> 00:08:11.374
of the evidence a systematic review would include in a 7,354 trial corpus, compared with 45% for

00:08:11.374 --> 00:08:16.914
label search alone. The two-stage design supports broad candidate retrieval followed by query

00:08:16.914 --> 00:08:22.555
specific filtering at rising per query cost with depth. Across the rest of the slate,

00:08:22.915 --> 00:08:27.715
RECOPPI produces relation grounded contextual, personally identifiable information,

00:08:28.195 --> 00:08:34.975
or PII, masking data for Korean documents that yields 88.42% annotator agreement on

00:08:34.975 --> 00:08:42.255
keep labels, versus 26.27% for author-based augmentation, and supports joint fine-tuning that

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:47.415
limits overmasking to at most 5.04% within a fixed leakage budget.

00:08:48.075 --> 00:08:53.895
Analysis of 10,420 congressional e-newsletters finds Democrats and Republicans surround the

00:08:53.895 --> 00:08:59.115
same election integrity terms with entirely different neighboring language, with divergence

00:08:59.115 --> 00:09:03.935
growing on certification after 2020, and on rigged install and after that year.

00:09:04.515 --> 00:09:09.475
A label preserving perturbation framework detects input ambiguity before disambiguation,

00:09:09.475 --> 00:09:15.595
and outperforms output site uncertainty baselines and LLM paraphrase baselines across open domain,

00:09:16.135 --> 00:09:21.815
conversational, and visual question answering data sets. A single JIS 6.7 billion

00:09:21.815 --> 00:09:28.555
parameter backbone fine-tuned with 4-bit quantized low-rank adaptation or Q-Lora ranks first on

00:09:28.555 --> 00:09:37.835
both the binary safe unsafe track at macro F1 0.984 and the 7-way harm domain track at macro F1 0.790

00:09:37.835 --> 00:09:44.195
of the R-Guard 2026 shared task while remaining accurate across six aerobic dialects.

00:09:44.675 --> 00:09:49.315
Lotus summarizes variable-length token representations with statistical descriptors,

00:09:49.615 --> 00:09:54.835
then applies low-rank multi-linear decomposition to train a lightweight hallucination classifier

00:09:54.835 --> 00:10:00.875
that improves over recent state-of-the-art baselines across multiple LLMs and question-answering benchmarks.

